# .graphifyignore
# Mirrors .gitignore syntax — tells graphify what NOT to index when building
# the knowledge graph. Excludes noisy/large/sensitive paths to keep token
# usage efficient and the graph focused on your actual business logic.
#
# WHY THIS MATTERS:
#   - Bytecode stripping: Hardhat/Foundry output massive metadata files per
#     compiled contract. Hiding artifacts/ + out/ stops Claude from parsing
#     thousands of lines of raw cryptographic bytecode.
#   - Token economy: Pruning node_modules/ + framework caches ensures graphify
#     builds its memory map exclusively on your custom logic — reduces initial
#     startup time and costs during active Claude Code sessions.
#   - Security: Never let .env files or credential paths enter the graph.
#
# VERSION NOTES (for awareness when upgrading graphifyy):
#   v0.4.1:  Fixed indexing engine crashes caused by tracking skipped ignore rules
#   v0.4.26: Resolved relative path matching bugs with ./raw directory expressions
#   v0.6.8:  Corrected strict behavior for folder-nested whitelist patterns (!src/**)
#
# USAGE: place in repo root. Use !path to whitelist exceptions to the rules above.
# Deploy from: ~/code/my-template/.graphifyignore (canonical source)

# ==============================================================================
# 1. DEPENDENCY TREES — biggest token savers
#    These directories contain thousands of third-party files that add zero
#    signal about your custom logic and will bloat the graph significantly.
# ==============================================================================
node_modules/
bower_components/
jspm_packages/
vendor/
.pnp
.pnp.js

# ==============================================================================
# 2. BUILD ARTIFACTS & OUTPUT BINARIES
#    Compiled output belongs in the graph only if it IS your primary artifact.
#    For most repos, strip it — source code tells the story better.
# ==============================================================================
dist/
build/
out/
target/
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# ==============================================================================
# 3. SMART CONTRACT BUILD ARTIFACTS (Web3 / Blockchain / DApp)
#    Hardhat and Foundry output massive metadata files containing raw bytecode,
#    ABI data, and ASTs for each compiled contract. These stop Claude from
#    parsing thousands of lines of raw cryptographic bytecode.
#
#    ABI PRESERVATION NOTE: when Claude needs an ABI to connect your JS
#    frontend to Solidity backend, reference the specific file path directly
#    in your prompt rather than indexing the entire cache directory.
# ==============================================================================
artifacts/
cache/
typechain/
typechain-types/
crytic-export/
.openzeppelin/

# ==============================================================================
# 4. FRONTEND CACHE & FRAMEWORK OUTPUT
#    Framework build caches, SSR output, and bundler artifacts add no signal.
# ==============================================================================
.next/
.nuxt/
.parcel-cache/
.cache/
.svelte-kit/

# ==============================================================================
# 5. SENSITIVE ENVIRONMENTS & LOCAL DATA
#    Never index secrets, credentials, or environment configs.
#    For agent-heavy / private repos this is the most critical section.
# ==============================================================================
.env
.env.*
.env.local
.env.development.local
.env.test.local
.env.production.local
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
secrets/
.secrets/

# ==============================================================================
# 6. LOG FILES — high noise, low signal
# ==============================================================================
*.log
logs/
*.log.*

# ==============================================================================
# 7. GRAPHIFY OWN OUTPUT — prevents circular self-reference
#    Always exclude graphify-out/ from its own indexing to avoid graph loops.
#
#    .GITIGNORE NOTE: separately add the following to .gitignore (not here):
#      graphify-out/manifest.json   ← file mtimes, breaks after git clone
#      graphify-out/cost.json       ← local API cost log only
#    These ARE worth committing: graph.json, GRAPH_REPORT.md, graph.html
# ==============================================================================
graphify-out/
.graphify_python
manifest.json
cost.json

# ==============================================================================
# 8. OS / EDITOR ARTIFACTS
# ==============================================================================
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/settings.json

# ==============================================================================
# REPO-SPECIFIC OVERRIDES — add below when deploying to a specific repo
# ==============================================================================

# --- Agent-heavy / private repos (trading-assistant, divorce-custody) ---
# specs/              ← internal workflow specs
# sessions/           ← raw session transcripts
# strategies/         ← proprietary strategy reference material
# data/imports/       ← raw trade/financial data imports
# child-support/      ← sensitive case documents
# custody/            ← sensitive case documents

# --- AI / Claude Code repos ---
# .claude/projects/   ← local project state
# .claude/memory/     ← local memory files
# AGENT-SYNC/         ← cross-agent handoff files

# ==============================================================================
# WHITELIST EXCEPTIONS — uncomment/add as needed
# Use ! prefix to force-include paths excluded above.
#
# Keep core Solidity source visible:
#   !contracts/**/*.sol
#   !src/**/*.js
#   !src/**/*.html
#
# For high-sensitivity repos — invert and only index source:
#   *
#   !src/
#   !src/**
# ==============================================================================
